  "correction_rules": [
    "Adjust forecasts downward when sentiment history includes positive sentiment (≥0.25) and model overestimates prices.",
    "Apply mean reversion bias correction: if forecast is > 10% above recent 5-day average, reduce by 5-10%.",
    "Reduce forecast overshoot after sharp upward spikes (e.g., >15% from prior day) by 10-20% to avoid overreaction.",
    "Increase forecast sensitivity to recent true outcomes when sentiment is neutral (0.00) — model should align more closely with actual price movements.",
    "Correct for lagged bias: if model consistently underestimates prices in early days of a 30-day forecast, add 2-5% to forecast for the first 5 days.",
    "When sentiment history shows no recent volatility (all 0.00), apply a conservative correction: reduce forecast by 1-3% to avoid overconfidence."
  ]
}
